# Git Workflow

Branch + PR for every change. Direct pushes to `main` are prohibited.

## Hard rules — never violate without explicit user override

1. **Never commit on `main`.** Before any commit, run `git branch --show-current`;
   if it's `main`, `git switch -c <type>/<slug> origin/main` first.
2. **Never `git push origin main`.** Push feature branches only
   (`git push -u origin HEAD` after `git switch -c`).
3. **Never `git push --force` to `main`** (not even `--force-with-lease`). On feature
   branches, `--force-with-lease` after rebase is fine.
4. **Never rewrite `main`'s history** — no interactive rebase, hard reset, or filter of `main`.

## Branch naming

`<type>/<kebab-slug>` — Conventional Commits types: `feat` `fix` `docs` `refactor`
`test` `build` `ci` `perf` `style` `chore` `revert`.

## PR flow

1. `gh pr create --fill` (title MUST be Conventional Commits format).
2. Merge with squash: `gh pr merge --squash --delete-branch`.

## Self-merge policy

| PR scope | Agent may self-merge? |
|---|---|
| Doc-only (no code) | Yes, after explicit approval |
| Code / tests / config | No — wait for human approval |
| Agent rules | No — always wait for human approval |

When this rule conflicts with user intent, stop and surface it; offer the PR path as
default. Only bypass on unambiguous override.
